  "verbalization": "Mitomycin's relationship with prostate cells is supported by multiple pathways that converge on the same target. The evidence suggests that mitomycin acts as a target for several molecules, including (4R)-4-(6-methylhepta-1,5-dien-2-yl)-1-(4-methylpent-3-enyl)cyclohexene and Lysine-specific demethylase 4C, which in turn target prostate cells. This indicates that mitomycin may exert its effects through indirect mechanisms involving these molecules, which are themselves targets of other compounds. The presence of multiple pathways pointing to prostate cells as a target suggests a broader role for mitomycin in interacting with cellular processes, possibly through the modulation of enzymatic activities or signaling pathways. The integration of these findings highlights a potential mechanism by which mitomycin influences prostate cell behavior, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
